Yaping He is a senior pharmacist and research scientist in the First Affiliated Hospital of Zhengzhou University. She received her Ph.D. degree in 2020 from Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences under the supervision of Prof. Jiwen Zhang. Her current research interest is the design of multifunctional drug delivery systems and nanomedicines based on new carriers of metal-organic frameworks.
Xiaojian Zhang is a professor and the director of Department of Pharmacy of the First Affiliated Hospital of Zhengzhou University, the office director of Hospital National Drug Clinical Trial Institution. He is secretary general of Clinical Pharmacy Branch, Chinese Medical Association. His research interests include precision clinical pharmacy, pharmacodynamic substance basis of traditional Chinese medicine, nanomedicine research and clinical translation.
Laurence H. Patterson is professor emeritus of drug discovery and former Director of the Institute of Cancer Therapeutics, University of Bradford, UK and a visiting professor to the Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences since 2010. He has over 30 years of experience in discovery and development of novel therapeutics, formulations and solutions for imaging, cytometry and drug screening.
Jiwen Zhang serves as the principal investigator in Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences. His team is specialized in supramolecular systems of cyclodextrin metalorganic frameworks and their derivatives, for controlled release and targeted drug delivery systems. Primarily using synchrotron quantitative methods characterizing the irregular and dynamic structures of drug delivery systems, his team and collaborators started a new area as Structure Pharmaceutics, focusing on the 3D structure of dosage forms and particulate systems.
